course: dictionary
lesson: 3243
title: What is an enzyme?
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An enzyme is a substance made by living things. Its job is to speed up chemical changes, which means it helps reactions happen faster. Your stomach uses enzymes to break your food into small pieces your body can use.
explain: Look for the clues in the sentences. «A cut apple goes brown because air reaches its chemicals and an enzyme helps them react with oxygen.» The enzyme is the helper that makes the reaction happen. Ask yourself: what is it helping to do?
explain: Enzymes are fussy about heat. They work best at certain temperatures, and too much heat stops them working. «Many modern washing powders work well at 30 °C» because their enzymes still work well at that lower temperature.
fact: An enzyme is a substance made by living things.
fact: Enzymes speed up chemical changes.
fact: Digestive enzymes in your saliva and stomach break food into small pieces.
fact: «Washing powder contains enzymes that break down protein and fat stains.»
fact: Enzymes work best at certain temperatures; too much heat stops them working.
exercise: «A cut apple goes brown because an enzyme helps air react with its chemicals.» What is an enzyme? | *A substance made by living things that speeds up chemical changes | A type of gas in the air | A sort of fruit that goes brown | A machine for cutting apples
exercise: «A squeeze of lemon slows it, because the acid stops the enzyme working well.» What does the lemon do to the browning apple? | *Slows it down | Makes the apple sweeter | Speeds it up | Stops the apple being cut
exercise: «Many modern washing powders work well at 30 °C and save energy.» Why is this useful? | It stops the enzymes working | It makes the powder boil | *It saves energy, because it works well at a lower temperature | It makes stains darker
test: «Bees make honey from nectar by adding enzymes.» What do bees add to nectar? | Washing powder | Water | Oxygen | *Enzymes
test: What is the job of enzymes in washing powder? | Making clothes warm | Drying the clothes | Adding bright colour | *Breaking down protein and fat stains
exam: Which sentence best describes an enzyme? | *A substance made by living things that speeds up chemical changes | A kind of stain on clothes | A metal used in cooking | A temperature that kills germs
